      "exercise": 629,
      "source_refs": ["p0207#12"],
      "status": "SOLVED_WITH_DECLARED_APPROXIMATIONS",
      "domain": "x in R; y=1.5^x has range (0,+infinity).",
      "source_task": "Construct y=1.5^x; obtain four function values, exponents giving 1,2,3,4,5, and roots of 1.5^x=5 and 1.5^x=7.5.",
      "graph_construction": [
        "Use horizontal x and vertical y axes; plot (-3,8/27), (-2,4/9), (-1,2/3), (0,1), (1,3/2), (2,9/4), (3,27/8), (4,81/16), (5,243/32). All these coordinates are exact.",
        "Join them with a smooth increasing exponential curve, positive everywhere, approaching y=0 as x tends to -infinity. Extending x through 5 and y through 8 covers the requested horizontal levels.",
        "For section 1, draw a vertical line at each requested x and read the intersection height. For sections 2 and 3, draw a horizontal line at each target height and read the unique intersection's x coordinate."
      ],
      "parts": [
        {"section": 1, "part": 1, "source_expression": "1.5^0.5", "exact_result": "sqrt(6)/2", "computed_value": 1.224744871391589, "chosen_graph_approximation": 1.22, "derivation": "(3/2)^(1/2)=sqrt(6)/2."},
        {"section": 1, "part": 2, "source_expression": "1.5^2.5", "exact_result": "9*sqrt(6)/8", "computed_value": 2.7556759606310752, "chosen_graph_approximation": 2.76, "derivation": "(3/2)^(5/2)=(9/4)*sqrt(6)/2."},
        {"section": 1, "part": 3, "source_expression": "1.5^(-0.5)", "exact_result": "sqrt(6)/3", "computed_value": 0.816496580927726, "chosen_graph_approximation": 0.82, "derivation": "(3/2)^(-1/2)=sqrt(2/3)=sqrt(6)/3."},
        {"section": 1, "part": 4, "source_expression": "1.5^(-1.5)", "exact_result": "2*sqrt(6)/9", "computed_value": 0.5443310539518174, "chosen_graph_approximation": 0.54, "derivation": "(3/2)^(-3/2)=(2/3)*sqrt(2/3)."},
        {"section": 2, "part": 1, "source_expression": "1.5^x=1", "exact_result": "x=0", "chosen_graph_approximation": 0, "derivation": "1.5^0=1; strict increase gives uniqueness."},
        {"section": 2, "part": 2, "source_expression": "1.5^x=2", "exact_result": "x=ln(2)/ln(3/2)", "computed_value": 1.7095112913514547, "chosen_graph_approximation": 1.71, "derivation": "Take logarithms; alternatively read the horizontal level y=2. It lies between x=1 and x=2."},
        {"section": 2, "part": 3, "source_expression": "1.5^x=3", "exact_result": "x=ln(3)/ln(3/2)", "computed_value": 2.7095112913514545, "chosen_graph_approximation": 2.71, "derivation": "Read y=3 between x=2 and x=3. Since 3=(3/2)*2, this exponent is exactly one more than the preceding one."},
        {"section": 2, "part": 4, "source_expression": "1.5^x=4", "exact_result": "x=ln(4)/ln(3/2)", "computed_value": 3.4190225827029095, "chosen_graph_approximation": 3.42, "derivation": "Read y=4 between x=3 and x=4, or use the logarithmic equation."},
        {"section": 2, "part": 5, "source_expression": "1.5^x=5", "exact_result": "x=ln(5)/ln(3/2)", "computed_value": 3.9693622959161177, "chosen_graph_approximation": 3.97, "derivation": "Read y=5 between x=3 and x=4, close to x=4 because 1.5^4=81/16=5.0625."},
        {"section": 3, "part": 1, "source_expression": "1.5^x=5", "exact_result": "{ln(5)/ln(3/2)}", "computed_value": 3.9693622959161177, "chosen_graph_approximation": 3.97, "derivation": "Same horizontal intersection as section 2 part 5; the real root is unique."},
        {"section": 3, "part": 2, "source_expression": "1.5^x=7.5", "exact_result": "{ln(15/2)/ln(3/2)}", "computed_value": 4.969362295916118, "chosen_graph_approximation": 4.97, "derivation": "7.5=(3/2)*5, so its exponent is exactly one more than the root for 5. The graph intersects this level between x=4 and x=5."}
      ],
      "uncertainty": "None in exact values or unique roots. Rounded decimals are chosen graph approximations only; source graph resolution is unspecified."
